{"event_id":"aab1e611-22cf-4a08-8346-ca3e0a3c89e9","incident_id":"INC-001","event_type":"DiagnosisCreated","timestamp":"2026-09-26T10:58:37.410Z","payload":{"evidence_ids":["INC-001:git_diff","INC-001:metrics","INC-001:trace","INC-001:logs"],"confidence":0.95,"root_cause":"A configuration change to the payment-service database connection pool (commit at 2026-09-26T09:05:00Z, config/payment-service.yaml) reduced max_connections from 50 to 5 while leaving acquire_timeout_ms at 2000. Once deployed, the pool was capped at 5 active connections: metrics show active connections dropping from 18 to 5, waiting requests climbing from 0 to 11 and then 17, and db_request_p95_ms ballooning from 42ms to 1900ms while db_query_p95_ms stayed flat at ~38-41ms, proving the bottleneck is connection acquisition, not query execution. Traces confirm it: req-0043's db.acquire_connection span ran the full 2000ms and errored with 'connection acquisition exceeded 2000 ms', and logs show 'database connection timeout after 2000 ms' for req-0042/req-0043 followed by 'POST /payments completed with HTTP 500'. Pool exhaustion caused requests to time out waiting for connections, surfacing as HTTP 500s (http_5xx_rate reached 8% by 09:07:30Z)."}}
